 ## Hard-won gotchas (July 2026 incident)
 - The Lovable build injects VITE_SUPABASE_* env vars that point at a DELETED project (pzzadswiradjnvvfybol). Never read those env vars. `client.ts` hardcodes the live project URL + anon key on purpose, and all edge-function fetches use the same hardcoded values. If you add code that calls Supabase, import SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY from `@/integrations/supabase/client`.
-- All 22 edge functions are deployed on flawuiqbvjobmkfkauhw (deployed 2026-07-01 via Supabase MCP from `supabase/functions/`). Redeploy through the MCP `deploy_edge_function` tool if they change.
+- All edge functions are deployed on flawuiqbvjobmkfkauhw via the Supabase MCP. The DEPLOYED source is the source of truth; `supabase/functions/` was re-synced to match on 2026-07-22 — keep it synced when redeploying, and redeploy through the MCP `deploy_edge_function` tool.
 - React error #310 on a game page means hooks after a conditional return. TransferPathBoard had this exact bug (early loading return above useState); the loading check must sit BELOW every hook.
+- VALIDATORS FAIL CLOSED (2026-07-22): every AI-backed grid/connect4 validator returns `{valid:false, unverified:true, reason:"…try again"}` when it cannot verify (Gemini quota, parse failure, error). Grid hooks treat `unverified` as a no-penalty retry (no guess burned); connect4/chain hooks reject-without-ending on network errors. NEVER reintroduce accept-on-error ("fail open") in a validator or its client catch — that was the July 2026 P1 (nonsense answers accepted while the free Gemini quota was exhausted).
+- Sandbox quirks (cost a session to diagnose): the Linux bash mount can serve STALE/TRUNCATED reads for repo files edited via the Write/Edit tools in the same session (a file ended mid-word under `tail` while the Read tool showed it complete) — trust Read/Grep for file content, never bash cat/grep, and don't panic over bogus "syntax errors" from bash-side compiles. Sandbox git can't use the index ("unknown index entry format") — use `git ls-remote` / `git cat-file` for remote truth and run the commit .bats Windows-side.
+- Tables created with CREATE TABLE AS (e.g. `*_bak_*` backups) have RLS OFF by default — a public-schema write hole via the anon key. Enable RLS immediately after creating any backup table (the 2026-07-22 baks were caught by `get_advisors` and locked down; advisors are worth running after any DDL).
 
 ## Database (Supabase)
 - Most game data lives in Postgres tables read via `src/lib/fetch*.ts` and game hooks.
